4. Git + Harness/CI-CD — Salesforce Validation | ~10 min

Imagine your PR contains:

AccountExplorerController.cls
AccountExplorerControllerTest.cls
accountExplorer LWC

A Salesforce CI pipeline shouldn't blindly push everything into production.

A simplified flow is:

Feature Branch
      ↓
Pull Request
      ↓
Static / quality checks
      ↓
Salesforce validation deployment
      ↓
Apex tests
      ↓
Code review / approvals
      ↓
Merge
      ↓
Deployment

A useful Salesforce CLI concept is a validation-only deployment.

The goal is essentially:

"Can this metadata deploy successfully
and do the required tests pass?"

without immediately committing the deployment.

Then production deployment happens after approval according to the team's process.

Harness can orchestrate stages around validation, approvals and deployment.

Deployment failure scenario

Suppose COMQA works, but SIT pipeline fails.

Don't immediately assume:

"My Apex is wrong."

Check:

Apex tests
Metadata dependencies
Custom metadata
Custom settings
Record types
Picklist configuration
Permission sets
Named Credentials
API versions
Environment-specific configuration

You've already hit a real example where a dependent picklist behaved correctly in COMQA but differently in SIT even though the frontend code looked right. That's exactly the kind of production-style debugging story you can eventually turn into a strong interview answer: verify the data/configuration layer before changing working application code.

A strong interview framework is:

Reproduce
   ↓
Compare environments
   ↓
Check logs
   ↓
Check metadata/config
   ↓
Identify difference
   ↓
Fix
   ↓
Regression test

